# Architecture

The repository is a PNPM workspace with two primary packages and infra assets.

- app/ — main Nuxt app (frontend + server/Nitro)
- microservice/ — maintenance companion
- .deploy/ — Kubernetes templates and profiles
- .github/workflows/ — CI: build, test, deploy
- scripts/ — local tooling, DB restore helpers, governance checks

## App package (Nuxt + Nitro)

Key top-level directories under app/:

- components/ — Vue components (AuthFormCard, modals for register entries, profile tabs, etc.)
- pages/ — standard Nuxt pages and large feature surfaces (account-registers, reoccurrences, reconciliation, admin/*)
- composables/ — client-side helpers (useAPI, useToday, useSnapshotMode, etc.)
- lib/ — shared utilities (auth, notifications, rounding, sorting, zod helpers)
- stores/ — Pinia stores (authStore, listStore)
- schema/ — Zod schemas (schema/zod.ts, schema/plaid.ts) with tests
- server/ — Nitro/H3 runtime (API, services, queues, cron, clients)
  - api/ — route handlers in method-suffixed files (e.g., login.post.ts). See api-surface.mdc
  - clients/ — prismaClient.ts, redisClient.ts, natsClient.ts, postmarkClient.ts, queuesClient.ts
  - services/ — business logic modules
    - forecast/* — ForecastEngine and collaborators (DataLoaderService, DateTimeService, ModernCacheService, etc.)
    - domain services: PlaidSyncService, TransactionMatchingService, CategoryReportService, ReoccurrenceHealth, etc.
  - queues/ — BullMQ queues (plaidSyncQueue, plaidSyncBalanceQueue, recalculateQueue, backupQueue)
  - cron/ — scheduled tasks (plaid.daily.ts, recalculate.hourly.ts, backup.daily.ts, crypto-balance.hourly.ts)
  - middleware/ — auth, sitemap redirect
  - routes/health — live.get.ts, ready.get.ts
  - lib/ — server helpers (auth/session, account access, error handling, rate limiting, plaid webhook integration, admin audit, etc.)
  - plugins/ — graceful shutdown, security headers, test date init
  - env.ts / envSchema.ts — runtime environment parsing/validation
- prisma/ — database schema, migrations, generated reencrypt/ helper code, seed.ts
- public/ — static files (favicon, robots.txt)
- tests/ —
  - e2e/ (Playwright specs and snapshots)
  - server/api/__tests__/ (comprehensive API/unit tests)
  - server/services/**/__tests__/ (service tests)
  - lib/__tests__/ and schema/__tests__/

Data flow in the app:

- UI (components/pages) → composables/stores → fetch to server/api/* → validate inputs (schema/zod) → delegate to server/services/* → server/clients/prismaClient.ts for DB, redisClient.ts for cache/queues → optional background queues for long-running work → HTTP response

Forecast engine flow (see forecast-engine.mdc):

- ForecastEngine orchestrates domain services (Registers, Reoccurrences, LoanCalculatorService, TransferService, DateTimeService, ModernCacheService, DataLoaderService, DataPersisterService). Test suite is large with integration and regression tests.

## Microservice package

- server.ts — H3/Nitro-like server bootstrap
- routes/ — migrate.get.ts, migrate.post.ts, test.get.ts (maintenance endpoints)
- clients/ — prismaClient.ts, redisClient.ts
- prisma/ — schema subset + reencrypt/ + migrations (mirrors main for relevant models)
- lib/bull.ts — BullMQ utilities
- scripts/k8s-rotate-db-key.sh — used in a special key-rotation image variant

Role: maintenance tasks like DB field-encryption key rotation and migration assistance. Deployed with a distinct Service and port (K8S sets containerPort 3050). See deployment.mdc and encryption-and-keys.mdc.

## Infrastructure

- Dockerfiles for app and microservice (multi-stage builds; Prisma generate at build time with placeholder DATABASE_URL)
- docker-compose.yaml — local MySQL and Redis services
- .deploy/*.template.yaml — manifests for main app, microservice, Service/Ingress, and a staged key-rotation CronJob + RBAC
- GitHub Actions — builds images to gcr.io and deploys to GKE (PR → staging, main → production)

## Cross-cutting concerns

- Validation: Zod schemas (app/schema/*.ts)
- Error handling: server/lib/handleApiError.ts + withErrorHandler.ts; userFriendlyApiError for UX
- Auth: server/middleware/auth.ts, server/lib/getUser.ts, accountAccess.ts, accountMembership.ts; TOTP/passkey/email MFA endpoints
- Logging: server/logger.ts (GCP logging integrations exist in devDependencies); admin audit and integration job logs
- Rate limiting: server/lib/rateLimitRedis.ts
- Encryption: prisma-field-encryption annotations in schema.prisma; RSA model and RsaService; see encryption-and-keys.mdc
